WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.000
While there's never any shortage of shows
to binge on Netflix, the streaming service

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.359
also boasts a massive, ever-changing selection
of movies.

00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:11.142
But it's all too easy to take a chance on
a new film, only to realize how bad it is

00:00:11.142 --> 00:00:12.142
halfway through.

00:00:12.142 --> 00:00:13.142
"Hey guys"

00:00:13.142 --> 00:00:14.140
"What?"

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.400
"What if the movie sucks?"

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.840
With that in mind, we rounded up a handful
of hidden gems on Netflix to make sure your

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.789
movie night is suck-free.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.070
Movies like...

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.369
The Voices

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:31.199
Released in 2014, The Voices tells the tale
of a guy named Jerry, played by Ryan Reynolds,

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:34.170
who lives a simple but lonely life as a factory
worker.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:38.860
His only real friends are his cat, his dog,
and his psychopathic urges.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:43.320
It's a seriously dark, twisted comedy anchored
by Reynolds' performance as a troubled but

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.300
cheerful guy who's so out of touch with reality
that even he can't believe some of the stuff

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.300
he's doing.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.840
Obviously, Ryan Reynolds isn't known for his
horror movies.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:55.150
If you've seen the 2005 Amityville Horror
remake and find it hard to believe that Reynolds

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:59.110
could play both funny and a legitimate creep,
you should give The Voices a watch.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.200
"You have the greatest hair, Tom.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:03.960
In the back.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:04.880
It's awesome."

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.560
Snow on Tha Bluff

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:11.160
Even though it's labeled as a documentary,
Snow on Tha Bluff is actually a "found-footage"

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.630
reality film that follows Curtis Snow, a real-life
armed robber.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:18.360
After Snow steals a camera from some naive
college students, he hands it to a buddy and

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.799
tells him to start filming.

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:23.450
Even though it's not truly a documentary,
Snow on Tha Bluff gives the audience a chilling

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.400
look at the gritty reality of life on the
street from Snow's perspective.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.140
While the footage is mostly dramatized, Curtis
Snow himself is very real and the situations

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.100
he faces are a daily reality for many.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.740
The Invitation

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.150
It's hard to talk about The Invitation without
spoiling the best parts, so we'll leave it

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:42.939
at this: if there was ever a dinner party
that went downhill, it's this one.

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:46.840
Director Karyn Kusama loads the movie with
tension right from the start and builds the

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.180
drama in a way that leaves you guessing right
along with the characters.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:54.640
With great, low-key performances from Michiel
Huisman and Logan Marshall-Green, The Invitation

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.520
is a swan dive into paranoia.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:00.899
It's also a welcome change of pace for Kusama,
whose previous films, Jennifer's Body and

00:02:00.899 --> 00:02:05.549
Aeon Flux, weren't exactly gems themselves,
hidden or otherwise.

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:06.810
Spectral

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.119
Sci-fi thrillers with style are hard to come
by.

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:12.359
If that's your kind of thing, chances are
you've seen all the good ones—and way too

00:02:12.359 --> 00:02:15.709
many bad ones—which makes Spectral even
more of a treat.

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:19.450
Following a team of U.S. Special Forces who
stumble across a mysterious new enemy while

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.639
on assignment in Moldova, Spectral jacks the
action into the stratosphere with lightning-quick

00:02:23.639 --> 00:02:26.969
combat scenes and several nail-biting moments
of true terror.

00:02:26.969 --> 00:02:30.609
Spectral isn't perfect, but it delivers what
it promises: a bunch of dudes fighting for

00:02:30.609 --> 00:02:32.709
their lives against an otherworldly threat.

00:02:32.709 --> 00:02:36.180
Stick it on, crank up the volume, and enjoy
the ride.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.069
The Midnight Meat Train

00:02:38.069 --> 00:02:42.340
Based on a short story by horror legend Clive
Barker, The Midnight Meat Train is straightforward

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.829
and extremely violent.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:47.269
It follows a struggling photographer, played
by Bradley Cooper, who uncovers some weird

00:02:47.269 --> 00:02:49.930
goings-on in a New York subway station late
at night.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.189
Convinced there's a killer on the loose even
though nobody else believes him, he decides

00:02:53.189 --> 00:02:57.280
to dig deeper on his own, and finds himself
drawn into an underground world darker than

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.809
he could have imagined.

00:02:58.809 --> 00:03:02.639
Unfortunately, some changes at Lionsgate during
the movie's release all but guaranteed that

00:03:02.639 --> 00:03:04.140
nobody would see the film.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.140
According to Barker, the studio opted to give
The Midnight Meat Train a very limited release

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:12.850
in second-rate theaters in favor of promoting
their other titles, like The Strangers, released

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:13.850
the same year.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:14.850
The result?

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:19.920
The $15 million picture brought back only
$83,000 and then quietly drifted away into

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.920
obscurity.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.590
Queue it up on Netflix and give it the attention
it deserves, because this is honestly one

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.799
of the best thrillers on the service right
now.

00:03:26.799 --> 00:03:27.799
Thanks for watching!

00:03:27.799 --> 00:03:30.079
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:30.079 --> 00:03:32.029
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

